1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 c5 4. dxc5 Nc6 5. Bb5 e6 6. b4 Bd7 7. Bxc6 Bxc6 8. a4
a5 9. b5 Bd7 10. Ba3 Qc7 11. Nf3 Bxc5 12. O-O Ne7 13. Nbd2 Rc8 14. Bxc5 Qxc5
15. Nb3 Qb4 16. Nfd4 O-O 17. Qe1 Qxe1 18. Rfxe1 b6 19. Nd2 Rc3 20. Re3 Rxe3 21.
fxe3 Nf5 22. Ra3 Rc8 23. c4 dxc4 24. Rc3 Rc5 25. N4f3 Bc8 26. e4 Ne7 27. Rxc4
Bb7 28. Rd4 $18 Ng6 29. Rd8+ (29. Nc4 $18) 29... Nf8 30. Rb8 $6 Rc7 31. Rd8 Rd7
32. Rxd7 $2 Nxd7 $15 33. Kf2 Nc5 34. Ke3 Nxa4 35. Nc4 h6 36. Nfd2 Kf8 37. Kd4
f5 38. exf5 Bxg2 39. fxe6 Ke7 40. Nd6 Kxe6 41. N2c4 g6 42. Ne3 Bf3 43. Nec4 g5
44. Ne3 h5 45. Nef5 Bg4 46. Ne3 Bf3 47. Nef5 Bg4 48. Ng3 Nc5 49. Nc4 Nd7 50.
Ne4 Kf5 51. Ne3+ Kg6 $2 52. Nxg4 hxg4 53. e6 (53. Kd5 $18) 53... Nf6 54. Nd6
Ng8 55. Nc8 ({In view of the inexplicable play of the next few moves, I'm
wondering if the game actually continued} 55. Nc4 Kf6 {- a mistake but an
understandable one -} 56. Kd5 Ne7+ 57. Kd6 Nc8+ 58. Kd7 a4 59. Nd6 Ne7 {
, reaching the position given in the score but with fewer obvious blunders})
55... Kf6 56. Kd5 $4 Ne7+ 57. Kd6 a4 $4 (57... Nxc8+ {is a ridiculously easy
win for Black, which suggests that there may be an error in the score
somewhere. Even more so, the four consecutive double question mark moves which
follow. See possible reconstruction given in the above note.}) 58. Kd7 $4 Nd5
$4 59. Nd6 $4 Ne7 $4 60. Ne4+ Kg7 61. Kxe7 a3 62. Kd6 a2 63. e7 a1=Q 64. e8=Q
Qh1 {"White won eventually" (bulletin). I've a strong feeling the score may be
wrong somewhere - JS} 1-0

